\description{
A \emph{bundle} is one file that holds the \strong{raw} API payloads of every session
a person has collected, so the same history can be loaded in R and in the
browser app without a database. It is a gzip-compressed JSON document:
}
\details{
\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode">}}\preformatted{\{ "schema_version": 1,
  "sessions": [ \{ "match_id": 123, "fetched_at": "...", "token": "...",
                  "match": <payload>, "stats": <payload>, "shots": <payload> \} ] \}
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

The three payloads are stored exactly as the share API returned them
(\verb{/matches/\{token\}}, \verb{/matches/\{token\}/stats}, \verb{/matches/\{token\}/shots}), so
every derived value can be recomputed with the current parsers and rules and
nothing is lost to an early parse. Numbers round-trip to 15 significant
digits. \code{token} is optional and only recorded when you supply it.\tabular{ll}{
   Function \tab Purpose \cr
   \code{bundle_new()} \tab An empty bundle \cr
   \code{bundle_read()}, \code{bundle_write()} \tab Read and write a bundle file \cr
   \code{bundle_payload_kind()} \tab Tell a match, stats or shots payload apart by content \cr
   \code{bundle_add_raw()} \tab Add one session from its three saved payloads \cr
   \code{bundle_merge()} \tab Merge two bundles by \code{match_id} \cr
   \code{bundle_players()} \tab Player names found in a bundle \cr
   \code{bundle_to_tables()} \tab Parse a bundle into the tables the metrics read \cr
   \code{bundle_derived()} \tab The derived-data interface, from those tables \cr
}


\code{bundle_to_tables()} and \code{bundle_derived()} need no database: they are what
the browser app runs.
}
\section{Bundle schema version}{

\code{schema_version} (see \code{\link[=bundle_schema_version]{bundle_schema_version()}}) is the version of the file
format, separate from \code{\link[=rallyr_schema_version]{rallyr_schema_version()}}. A file with a higher
version than this package supports is refused, never read partly.
}

